WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.186
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level three.

2
00:00:06.486 --> 00:00:09.571
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.871 --> 00:00:16.935
Unit twenty-two: Environmental Policy. Today you will compare ideas with not so much ... as and as much as.

4
00:00:17.235 --> 00:00:19.957
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:24.342
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.183 --> 00:00:27.113
Environmental policy.

7
00:00:28.117 --> 00:00:32.345
Environmental policy means government plans for protecting nature.

8
00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:36.587
Environmental policy now includes climate targets.

9
00:00:37.183 --> 00:00:40.962
Your turn. Say: Environmental policy.

10
00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:46.612
Environmental policy.

11
00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:48.525
Regulation.

12
00:00:49.517 --> 00:00:53.026
Regulation means an official rule made by a government body.

13
00:00:53.617 --> 00:00:56.313
A new regulation limits factory emissions.

14
00:00:56.917 --> 00:00:59.604
Your turn. Say: Regulation.

15
00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:03.746
Regulation.

16
00:01:04.483 --> 00:01:05.403
Pollution.

17
00:01:06.417 --> 00:01:10.390
Pollution means harmful substances in the air, water or soil.

18
00:01:10.983 --> 00:01:13.018
Pollution in the river killed the fish.

19
00:01:13.617 --> 00:01:16.292
Your turn. Say: Pollution.

20
00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:20.088
Pollution.

21
00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.385
Impact assessment.

22
00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:27.809
Impact assessment means an official study of the likely effects of a plan.

23
00:01:28.417 --> 00:01:31.391
An impact assessment is required before building.

24
00:01:31.983 --> 00:01:35.425
Your turn. Say: Impact assessment.

25
00:01:38.267 --> 00:01:39.918
Impact assessment.

26
00:01:40.683 --> 00:01:41.975
Protected area.

27
00:01:42.983 --> 00:01:46.573
Protected area means land or sea where nature is legally protected.

28
00:01:47.183 --> 00:01:49.821
The protected area shelters rare birds.

29
00:01:50.417 --> 00:01:53.092
Your turn. Say: Protected area.

30
00:01:55.933 --> 00:01:57.573
Protected area.

31
00:01:58.317 --> 00:01:59.434
Enforcement.

32
00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:03.436
Enforcement means making sure that people obey a law.

33
00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:07.048
Enforcement improved after inspectors were hired.

34
00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:10.186
Your turn. Say: Enforcement.

35
00:02:13.033 --> 00:02:14.255
Enforcement.

36
00:02:15.017 --> 00:02:16.598
Public consultation.

37
00:02:17.583 --> 00:02:21.766
Public consultation means a process of asking citizens for their views.

38
00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:24.837
Public consultation changed the route of the road.

39
00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:28.892
Your turn. Say: Public consultation.

40
00:02:31.733 --> 00:02:33.210
Public consultation.

41
00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:35.311
Sustainability.

42
00:02:36.317 --> 00:02:40.278
Sustainability means meeting present needs without harming the future.

43
00:02:40.883 --> 00:02:44.462
Sustainability guides the city's long-term plan.

44
00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:47.679
Your turn. Say: Sustainability.

45
00:02:50.533 --> 00:02:52.057
Sustainability.

46
00:02:52.867 --> 00:02:56.239
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:57.083 --> 00:03:03.532
Visal, an expert says 'The problem is not so much the law as its enforcement.' What does 'not so much... as' mean?

48
00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:17.079
It corrects an idea: the real issue is enforcement rather than the law itself. The structure is not so much A as B, where A is the weaker point and B is the more important one.

49
00:03:18.183 --> 00:03:20.218
Are there other comparison patterns?

50
00:03:21.317 --> 00:03:35.233
Yes: as much as shows equality (Enforcement matters as much as regulation). Not as/so ... as shows a difference. The more... the more shows a link, and twice as ... as gives a multiple.

51
00:03:36.317 --> 00:03:38.165
How do I use them for pollution?

52
00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:49.495
Pollution is not so much a technical problem as a political one. A protected area is only worth as much as the rangers who defend it.

53
00:03:50.633 --> 00:03:52.157
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:53.017 --> 00:03:58.221
Grammar focus: Comparison: not so much A as B and as much as.

55
00:03:58.521 --> 00:03:59.812
Look at the pattern.

56
00:04:00.517 --> 00:04:03.596
The problem is not so much the law as its enforcement.

57
00:04:04.483 --> 00:04:07.481
Enforcement matters as much as the regulation itself.

58
00:04:08.383 --> 00:04:11.730
Pollution is not so much a technical issue as a political one.

59
00:04:12.667 --> 00:04:23.707
Not so much A as B = B is the real point. As much as = equal importance. Not as / so + adjective + as = a lower degree. Use them to compare ideas clearly.

60
00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:28.101
Be careful! Don't say: Not so much a slogan than a habit.

61
00:04:30.067 --> 00:04:32.623
Say: Not so much a slogan as a habit.

62
00:04:32.923 --> 00:04:34.772
Use 'as' after 'not so much'.

63
00:04:35.567 --> 00:04:38.544
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:39.333 --> 00:04:41.797
Laws on Paper, Laws in Practice.

65
00:04:42.097 --> 00:04:47.789
Environmental policy often fails not so much because laws are weak as because enforcement is weak.

66
00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:53.609
A regulation on pollution is worth as much as the inspectors who check factories.

67
00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:59.665
An impact assessment is not as useful as it could be when public consultation is ignored.

68
00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:04.826
A protected area needs money and rangers as much as it needs a map.

69
00:05:05.833 --> 00:05:11.119
Sustainability, in the end, is not so much a slogan as a daily habit of government.

70
00:05:12.233 --> 00:05:16.235
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:17.083 --> 00:05:19.826
It is not so much the law blank its enforcement.

72
00:05:20.126 --> 00:05:23.048
A, than. B, as. C, but.

73
00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:28.681
The answer is B: as.

74
00:05:29.817 --> 00:05:32.165
Enforcement matters blank the regulation.

75
00:05:32.465 --> 00:05:36.455
A, as much as. B, so much as. C, much than.

76
00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:42.034
The answer is A: as much as.

77
00:05:43.183 --> 00:05:46.367
A place where nature is legally protected is a blank area.

78
00:05:46.667 --> 00:05:50.204
A, polluted. B, enforced. C, protected.

79
00:05:53.767 --> 00:05:56.010
The answer is C: protected.

80
00:05:57.150 --> 00:05:58.848
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:05:59.148 --> 00:06:06.354
A, Not so much a slogan than a habit.. B, Not so much a slogan as a habit.. C, Not much a slogan as a habit..

82
00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:13.467
The answer is B: Not so much a slogan as a habit..

83
00:06:14.617 --> 00:06:20.273
According to the reading, an impact assessment is less useful when public consultation is…

84
00:06:20.573 --> 00:06:23.844
A, ignored. B, complete. C, early.

85
00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:29.156
The answer is A: ignored.

86
00:06:30.367 --> 00:06:33.716
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:34.550 --> 00:06:37.490
Why is enforcement as important as the law itself?

88
00:06:46.283 --> 00:06:47.714
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:48.014 --> 00:07:12.986
A law that is not enforced has no practical effect. If factories can pollute without fines, they will treat the rule as optional, and honest companies are punished by unfair competition. Enforcement means inspectors, clear penalties and honest courts. It shows citizens that the law is serious, which builds trust and encourages voluntary compliance.

90
00:07:13.286 --> 00:07:14.810
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:15.717 --> 00:07:22.316
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and comparison: not so much a as b and as much as.

92
00:07:22.616 --> 00:07:28.578
Today's value is environmental stewardship. Care for nature as a trust for future generations.

93
00:07:28.878 --> 00:07:31.994
See you in Unit twenty-three. Goodbye!

94
00:07:32.294 --> 00:07:36.050
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

